osition":-1,"displayBars":50,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":"#af945f","background":"#af945f"},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":2,"texture":"modules/the-moonlit-march-module/ART/PLAYER%20CHARACTERS/TOKEN%20ART/DYNAMIC/DT_CALCIFER_YIZIN-MECHVIM_CLICKCLACK.webp"}},"turnMarker":{"mode":2,"animation":"spin","src":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/62465a9c3297d9e952a84538/marker06.webp","disposition":true},"movementAction":null,"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"name":"Calcifer (Familiar of Yizin)","type":"familiar","ownership":{"default":2,"rRqGmfO5dCn3oNkd":3,"Op1MRCz0XkfNZzms":3},"effects":[],"system":{"_migration":{"version":0.959,"previous":{"schema":0.955,"foundry":"14.361","system":"8.1.2"}},"master":{"id":"1Ke4AweM9VXNDscd","ability":"cha"},"attributes":{"hp":{"value":0,"temp":0}},"details":{"creature":{"value":"Bearded Dragon"}}},"_id":"nPvzphwjMfHWPqw8","img":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/65d7e46cc949d90930374730/modules/the-moonlit-march-module/ART/PLAYER%20CHARACTERS/FULL%20ART/FA_CALCIFER_YIZIN-MECHVIM_CLICKCLACK.webp","items":[{"_id":"7rDAtf8y3AP60IZn","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp","name":"Valet","system":{"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"familiar","description":{"value":"<p>You can command your familiar to deliver you items more efficiently. Your familiar doesn't use its 2 actions immediately upon your command. Instead, up to twice before the end of your turn, you can have your familiar Interact to retrieve an item of light or negligible Bulk you are wearing and place it into one of your free hands. The familiar can't use this ability to retrieve stowed items. If the familiar has a different number of actions, it can retrieve one item for each action it has when commanded this way.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"license":"ORC","remaster":true,"title":"Pathfinder Player Core","authors":""},"rules":[],"traits":{"value":[],"otherTags":[]},"slug":"valet","_migration":{"version":0.959,"previous":null}},"type":"action","_stats":{"coreVersion":"14.367","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"8.5.0","compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.familiar-abilities.Item.9PsptrEoCC4QdM23","createdTime":1789837471576,"modifiedTime":1789837471577,"lastModifiedBy":"Op1MRCz0XkfNZzms","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"Op1MRCz0XkfNZzms":3},"flags":{"pf2e-dailies":{"temporary":true}}},{"_id":"RQAqogKzU7SpvhXA","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp","name":"Familiar Focus","system":{"actionType":{"value":"action"},"actions":{"value":2},"category":"familiar","description":{"value":"<p>Once per day, your familiar can use 2 actions with the concentrate trait to restore 1 Focus Point to your focus pool, up to your usual maximum. You must have a focus pool to select this.</p>","gm":""},"frequency":{"max":1,"per":"day"},"publication":{"license":"ORC","remaster":true,"title":"Pathfinder Player Core","authors":""},"rules":[],"traits":{"value":[],"otherTags":[]},"slug":"familiar-focus","_migration":{"version":0.959,"previous":null}},"type":"action","_stats":{"coreVersion":"14.367","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"8.5.0","compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.familiar-abilities.Item.jdlefpPcSCIe27vO","createdTime":1789837471901,"modifiedTime":1789837471902,"lastModifiedBy":"Op1MRCz0XkfNZzms","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"Op1MRCz0XkfNZzms":3},"flags":{"pf2e-dailies":{"temporary":true}}},{"img":"systems/pf2e/icons/conditions/confused.webp","name":"Confused","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You don't have your wits about you, and you attack wildly. You are @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.AJh5ex99aV6VTggg]{Off-Guard}, you don't treat anyone as your ally (though they might still treat you as theirs), and you can't Delay, Ready, or use reactions.</p>\n<p>You use all your actions to Strike or cast offensive cantrips, though the GM can have you use other actions to facilitate attack, such as draw a weapon, move so target is in reach, and so forth. Your targets are determined randomly by the GM. If you have no other viable targets, you target yourself, automatically hitting but not scoring a critical hit. If it's impossible for you to attack or cast spells, you babble incoherently, wasting your actions.</p>\n<p>Each time you take damage from an attack or spell, you can attempt a @Check[flat|showDC:all|dc:11] to recover from your confusion and end the condition.</p>","gm":""},"group":null,"overrides":[],"publication":{"license":"ORC","remaster":true,"title":"Pathfinder Player Core","authors":""},"references":{"children":[],"overriddenBy":[],"overrides":[],"parent":null},"rules":[{"key":"ActiveEffectLike","mode":"override","path":"system.attributes.flanking.canFlank","value":false},{"key":"RollOption","option":"target:ally","value":false},{"key":"RollOption","option":"origin:ally","value":false},{"inMemoryOnly":true,"key":"GrantItem","uuid":"Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.AJh5ex99aV6VTggg"},{"key":"Note","predicate":[{"or":["item:type:spell","origin:action:trait:attack"]}],"selector":"damage-received","text":"PF2E.condition.confused.note","title":"{item|name}"}],"traits":{"value":[],"otherTags":[]},"value":{"isValued":false,"value":null},"slug":"confused","_migration":{"version":0.959,"previous":null},"fromSpell":false,"persistent":null},"type":"condition","_stats":{"coreVersion":"14.367","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"8.5.0","compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.yblD8fOR1J8rDwEQ","createdTime":1789857018121,"modifiedTime":1789857018122,"lastModifiedBy":"rRqGmfO5dCn3oNkd","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"rRqGmfO5dCn3oNkd":3},"flags":{},"_id":"5YPxECQ9k92wJ3py"},{"img":"systems/pf2e/icons/conditions/dying.webp","name":"Dying","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are bleeding out or otherwise at death's door. While you have this condition, you are @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fBnFDH2MTzgFijKf]{Unconscious}. Dying always includes a value, and if it ever reaches dying 4, you die. When you're dying, you must attempt a recovery check at the start of your turn each round to determine whether you get better or worse. Your dying condition increases by 1 if you take damage while dying, or by 2 if you take damage from an enemy's critical hit or a critical failure on your save.</p>\n<p>If you lose the dying condition by succeeding at a recovery check and are still at 0 Hit Points, you remain unconscious, but you can wake up as described in that condition. You lose the dying condition automatically and wake up if you ever have 1 Hit Point or more. Any time you lose the dying condition, you gain the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Yl48xTdMh3aeQYL2]{Wounded 1} condition, or increase your wounded condition value by 1 if you already have that condition.</p>","gm":""},"group":"death","overrides":[],"publication":{"license":"ORC","remaster":true,"title":"Pathfinder Player Core","authors":""},"references":{"children":[],"overriddenBy":[],"overrides":[],"parent":null},"rules":[{"key":"GrantItem","onDeleteActions":{"grantee":"restrict"},"uuid":"Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fBnFDH2MTzgFijKf","flag":"unconscious"}],"traits":{"value":[],"otherTags":[]},"value":{"isValued":true,"value":4},"slug":"dying","_migration":{"version":0.959,"previous":null},"fromSpell":false,"persistent":null},"type":"condition","_stats":{"coreVersion":"14.367","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"8.5.0","compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.yZRUzMqrMmfLu0V1","createdTime":1789858010210,"modifiedTime":1789859256488,"lastModifiedBy":"Op1MRCz0XkfNZzms","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"rRqGmfO5dCn3oNkd":3},"flags":{"pf2e":{"itemGrants":{"unconscious":{"id":"pyk7AgqDVam0NkQ8","onDelete":"restrict"}}}},"_id":"zUnEwNcAVH4QJGhx"},{"img":"systems/pf2e/icons/conditions/unconscious.webp","name":"Unconscious","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You're sleeping or have been knocked out. You can't act. You take a –4 status penalty to AC, Perception, and Reflex saves, and you have the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.XgEqL1kFApUbl5Z2]{Blinded} and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.AJh5ex99aV6VTggg]{Off-Guard} conditions. When you gain this condition, you fall @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.j91X7x0XSomq8d60]{Prone} and drop items you're holding unless the effect states otherwise or the GM determines you're positioned so you wouldn't.</p>\n<p>If you're unconscious because you're @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.yZRUzMqrMmfLu0V1]{Dying}, you can't wake up while you have 0 Hit Points. If you are restored to 1 Hit Point or more, you lose the dying and unconscious conditions and can act normally on your next turn.</p>\n<p>If you are unconscious and at 0 Hit Points, but not dying, you return to 1 Hit Point and awaken after sufficient time passes. The GM determines how long you remain unconscious, from a minimum of 10 minutes to several hours. If you are healed, you lose the unconscious condition and can act normally on your next turn.</p>\n<p>If you're unconscious and have more than 1 Hit Point (typically because you are asleep or unconscious due to an effect), you wake up in one of the following ways.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You take damage, though if the damage reduces you to 0 Hit Points, you remain unconscious and gain the dying condition as normal.</li>\n<li>You receive healing, other than the natural healing you get from resting.</li>\n<li>Someone shakes you awake with an @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.pvQ5rY2zrtPI614F]{Interact} action.</li>\n<li>Loud noise around you might wake you. At the start of your turn, you automatically attempt a Perception check against the noise's DC (or the lowest DC if there is more than one noise), waking up if you succeed. If creatures are attempting to stay quiet around you, this Perception check uses their Stealth DCs. Some effects make you sleep so deeply that they don't allow you this Perception check.</li>\n<li>If you are simply asleep, the GM decides you wake up either because you have had a restful night's sleep or something disrupted that rest.</li>\n</ul>","gm":""},"group":"death","overrides":[],"publication":{"license":"ORC","remaster":true,"title":"Pathfinder Player Core","authors":""},"references":{"children":[],"overriddenBy":[],"overrides":[],"parent":null},"rules":[{"key":"FlatModifier","selector":["ac","perception","reflex"],"slug":"unconscious","type":"status","value":-4},{"key":"GrantItem","onDeleteActions":{"grantee":"restrict"},"uuid":"Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.XgEqL1kFApUbl5Z2","flag":"blinded"},{"inMemoryOnly":true,"key":"GrantItem","uuid":"Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.AJh5ex99aV6VTggg"},{"allowDuplicate":false,"key":"GrantItem","onDeleteActions":{"grantee":"restrict","granter":"detach"},"uuid":"Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.j91X7x0XSomq8d60","flag":"prone"}],"traits":{"value":[],"otherTags":[]},"value":{"isValued":false,"value":null},"slug":"unconscious","_migration":{"version":0.959,"previous":null},"fromSpell":false,"persistent":null},"type":"condition","_stats":{"coreVersion":"14.367","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"8.5.0","compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fBnFDH2MTzgFijKf","createdTime":1789858010212,"modifiedTime":1789858010217,"lastModifiedBy":"rRqGmfO5dCn3oNkd","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"rRqGmfO5dCn3oNkd":3},"flags":{"pf2e":{"grantedBy":{"id":"zUnEwNcAVH4QJGhx","onDelete":"cascade"},"itemGrants":{"blinded":{"id":"wKAxXOVkKLvTOD92","onDelete":"restrict"},"prone":{"id":"vS7DqRbxZpRsvhNZ","onDelete":"restrict"}}}},"_id":"pyk7AgqDVam0NkQ8"},{"img":"systems/pf2e/icons/conditions/blinded.webp","name":"Blinded","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can't see. All normal terrain is difficult terrain to you. You can't detect anything using vision. You automatically critically fail Perception checks that require you to be able to see, and if vision is your only precise sense, you take a –4 status penalty to Perception checks. You are immune to visual effects. Blinded overrides @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.TkIyaNPgTZFBCCuh]{Dazzled}.</p>","gm":""},"group":"senses","overrides":["dazzled"],"publication":{"license":"ORC","remaster":true,"title":"Pathfinder Player Core","authors":""},"references":{"children":[],"overriddenBy":[],"overrides":[],"parent":null},"rules":[{"key":"FlatModifier","selector":"perception","slug":"blinded","type":"status","value":-4},{"key":"Immunity","type":"visual"}],"traits":{"value":[],"otherTags":[]},"value":{"isValued":false,"value":null},"slug":"blinded","_migration":{"version":0.959,"previous":null},"fromSpell":false,"persistent":null},"type":"condition","_stats":{"coreVersion":"14.367","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"8.5.0","compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.XgEqL1kFApUbl5Z2","createdTime":1789858010214,"modifiedTime":1789858010218,"lastModifiedBy":"rRqGmfO5dCn3oNkd","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"rRqGmfO5dCn3oNkd":3},"flags":{"pf2e":{"grantedBy":{"id":"pyk7AgqDVam0NkQ8","onDelete":"cascade"}}},"_id":"wKAxXOVkKLvTOD92"},{"img":"systems/pf2e/icons/conditions/prone.webp","name":"Prone","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You're lying on the ground. You are @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.AJh5ex99aV6VTggg]{Off-Guard} and take a –2 circumstance penalty to attack rolls. The only move actions you can use while you're prone are @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Tj055UcNm6UEgtCg]{Crawl} and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.OdIUybJ3ddfL7wzj]{Stand}. Standing up ends the prone condition. You can @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.ust1jJSCZQUhBZIz]{Take Cover} while prone to hunker down and gain greater cover against ranged attacks, even if you don't have an object to get behind, which grants you a +4 circumstance bonus to AC against ranged attacks (but you remain off-guard).</p>\n<p>If you would be knocked prone while you're @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.pprgrYQ1QnIDGZiy]{Climbing} or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.cS9nfDRGD83bNU1p]{Flying}, you fall. You can't be knocked prone when @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.c8TGiZ48ygoSPofx]{Swimming}.</p>","gm":""},"group":null,"overrides":[],"publication":{"license":"ORC","remaster":true,"title":"Pathfinder Player Core","authors":""},"references":{"children":[],"overriddenBy":[],"overrides":[],"parent":null},"rules":[{"key":"FlatModifier","selector":"attack-roll","slug":"prone","type":"circumstance","value":-2},{"inMemoryOnly":true,"key":"GrantItem","uuid":"Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.AJh5ex99aV6VTggg"}],"traits":{"value":[],"otherTags":[]},"value":{"isValued":false,"value":null},"slug":"prone","_migration":{"version":0.959,"previous":null},"fromSpell":false,"persistent":null},"type":"condition","_stats":{"coreVersion":"14.367","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"8.5.0","compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.j91X7x0XSomq8d60","createdTime":1789858010216,"modifiedTime":1789858010219,"lastModifiedBy":"rRqGmfO5dCn3oNkd","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"rRqGmfO5dCn3oNkd":3},"flags":{"pf2e":{"grantedBy":{"id":"pyk7AgqDVam0NkQ8","onDelete":"detach"}}},"_id":"vS7DqRbxZpRsvhNZ"},{"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/mouth-teeth-tongue-purple.webp","name":"Effect: Engulf and Swallow Whole","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Granted by @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.Item.zU3Ovaet4xQ5Gmvy]{Engulf} or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.Item.uJSseLa57HZYSMUu]{Swallow Whole}</p>\n<p>You are grabbed, slowed 1, and you have to hold your breath or start suffocating. You can only attack the origin with unarmed attacks or with weapons of light Bulk or less, and the origin is off-guard against the attack. If the origin takes piercing or slashing damage equaling or exceeding the listed Rupture value from a single attack or spell, you cut yourself free.</p>","gm":""},"duration":{"expiry":null,"sustained":false,"unit":"unlimited","value":-1},"level":{"value":1},"publication":{"license":"ORC","remaster":true,"title":"Pathfinder Monster Core","authors":""},"rules":[{"inMemoryOnly":true,"key":"GrantItem","uuid":"Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.kWc1fhmv9LBiTuei"},{"inMemoryOnly":true,"key":"GrantItem","uuid":"Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3"},{"key":"GrantItem","uuid":"Compendium.pf2e.other-effects.Item.2u26bmArDPuoCljc","flag":"effectRemainingAir"},{"key":"Note","predicate":[{"nor":["item:bulk:light","item:bulk:negligible","item:category:unarmed"]}],"selector":"strike-attack-roll","text":"PF2E.SpecificRule.SwallowWhole.InvalidAttack","title":"{item|name}"},{"key":"EphemeralEffect","predicate":["target:signature:{item|origin.signature}",{"or":["item:bulk:light","item:bulk:negligible","item:category:unarmed"]}],"selectors":"strike-attack-roll","uuid":"Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.AJh5ex99aV6VTggg"},{"key":"Note","predicate":[{"or":["item:type:spell",{"and":["item:type:weapon","target:signature:{item|origin.signature}",{"or":["item:bulk:light","item:bulk:negligible","item:category:unarmed"]}]}]},{"or":["item:damage:type:piercing","item:damage:type:slashing"]}],"selector":["strike-damage","spell-damage"],"text":"PF2E.SpecificRule.SwallowWhole.RuptureDamage","title":"{item|name}"}],"start":{"value":226310,"initiative":26},"tokenIcon":{"show":true},"traits":{"value":[],"otherTags":[]},"slug":"effect-engulf-and-swallow-whole","_migration":{"version":0.959,"previous":null},"unidentified":false,"badge":null,"fromSpell":false,"context":{"origin":{"actor":"Actor.TGf0JzBpliAKUFLp","token":null,"item":"Actor.TGf0JzBpliAKUFLp.Item.RWDHcA6Je7fFUmpG","spellcasting":null,"rollOptions":["origin:type:npc","origin:signature:b630b993-f192-5acf-bfcd-97740fbbec6e","origin:participant:initiative:roll:26","origin:participant:initiative:rank:4","origin:creature","origin:level:9","origin:caster","origin:caster:tradition:arcane","origin:condition:persistent-damage","origin:condition:persistent-damage:force","origin:effect:taunt","origin:condition:off-guard","origin:effect:taunt:f38fe9fe-5184-5e3d-9375-c82444be75f7","origin:trait:occult","origin:mode:living","origin:trait:arcane","origin:trait:dragon","origin:size:5","origin:size:gargantuan","origin:item:type:action","origin:item:id:RWDHcA6Je7fFUmpG","origin:item:engulf","origin:item:slug:engulf","origin:item:action:type:action","origin:item:action:cost:2"]},"target":null,"roll":null}},"type":"effect","_stats":{"coreVersion":"14.367","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"8.5.0","compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-effects.Item.1cbIe569UD6paXad","createdTime":1789858048380,"modifiedTime":1789858048383,"lastModifiedBy":"rRqGmfO5dCn3oNkd","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"rRqGmfO5dCn3oNkd":3},"flags":{"pf2e":{"itemGrants":{"effectRemainingAir":{"id":"8KIAQC0547UD98jl","onDelete":"detach"}}}},"_id":"YZM5AjmA7WJKUk1q"},{"img":"icons/magic/air/weather-wind-gust.webp","name":"Effect: Remaining Air","system":{"badge":{"max":600,"min":null,"type":"counter","value":600,"labels":null,"loop":false},"description":{"value":"<p>See @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.journals.JournalEntry.S55aqwWIzpQRFhcq.JournalEntryPage.OiRwxbfLNUniLg15#drowning-and-suffocating]{Drowning and Suffocating}</p>\n<p>You can hold your breath for a number of rounds equal to 5 + your Constitution modifier. Reduce your remaining air by 1 round at the end of each of your turns, or by 2 if you attacked or cast any spells that turn.</p>\n<p>You also lose 1 round worth of air each time you are critically hit or critically fail a save against a damaging effect. If you speak (including Casting a Spell) you lose all remaining air.</p>","gm":""},"duration":{"expiry":null,"sustained":false,"unit":"unlimited","value":-1},"level":{"value":1},"publication":{"license":"ORC","remaster":true,"title":"Pathfinder Player Core","authors":""},"rules":[{"key":"ActiveEffectLike","mode":"add","path":"flags.system.remainingAir.rounds","value":"5 + floor(@actor.abilities.con.mod)"},{"itemId":"{item|id}","key":"ItemAlteration","mode":"override","property":"badge-max","value":"@actor.flags.system.remainingAir.rounds"},{"key":"Note","selector":"attack","text":"PF2E.SpecificRule.RemainingAir.AttackOrSpells","title":"PF2E.SpecificRule.RemainingAir.Label"},{"itemType":"spell","key":"ItemAlteration","label":"PF2E.SpecificRule.RemainingAir.Label","mode":"add","priority":121,"property":"description","value":[{"text":"PF2E.SpecificRule.RemainingAir.AttackOrSpells"},{"predicate":[{"not":"item:trait:subtle"}],"text":"PF2E.SpecificRule.RemainingAir.Speak"}]},{"itemType":"action","key":"ItemAlteration","label":"PF2E.SpecificRule.RemainingAir.Label","mode":"add","predicate":["item:trait:auditory"],"priority":121,"property":"description","value":[{"text":"PF2E.SpecificRule.RemainingAir.Speak"}]},{"itemType":"feat","key":"ItemAlteration","label":"PF2E.SpecificRule.RemainingAir.Label","mode":"add","predicate":["item:trait:auditory"],"priority":121,"property":"description","value":[{"text":"PF2E.SpecificRule.RemainingAir.Speak"}]},{"key":"Note","outcome":["c